# ላቁም? in production: Caddy in front of everything (docs/DEPLOY.md).
#
# - HTTPS by itself: Let's Encrypt certificates for {$DOMAIN}, obtained and
#   renewed automatically. Free, and no account or card is needed.
# - One origin for the dashboard and the API, so there is no CORS, and the
#   driver app, Chapa's webhook and its return page all use the same name.
# - X-Forwarded-For: Caddy REPLACES whatever a client sent with the client's
#   real address ("to prevent spoofing", per its reverse_proxy docs), so the
#   API trusts exactly one hop: TRUST_PROXY_HOPS=1.
# - WebSockets (/socket.io) are proxied as they are, with no setting.

{$DOMAIN} {
	encode zstd gzip

	# The API's public surface. /health and /ready stay inside the compose
	# network: /ready describes the database and Redis, which is nobody's
	# business outside. /dev/* is never registered in production anyway.
	@api path /v1/* /socket.io/* /payment-complete
	handle @api {
		reverse_proxy api:3000
	}

	# The attendant dashboard: a single-page app, built into /srv.
	handle {
		root * /srv
		try_files {path} /index.html
		file_server
	}

	# Vite names every asset by its content, so they never change: cache them
	# for a year. index.html must always be fetched fresh, or a tablet keeps
	# an old dashboard after a deploy.
	@assets path /assets/*
	header @assets Cache-Control "public, max-age=31536000, immutable"
	@page path / /index.html
	header @page Cache-Control "no-cache"

	header {
		Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000"
		X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
		Referrer-Policy "strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
		-Server
	}
}
